Title: NIGHT SHIFT
Credit: Written by
Author: Jo Writer

INT. MARA'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Rain streaks the window.  MARA  (30s) stares at an  unplugged  phone, and the  well-known  silence of the room,  all of it , presses in.
She does not move.

MARA
(to herself)
He is not going to call. He is not going to call, and that is fine.

JONAH (V.O.)
Mara, it's me. I know it's late & I know you said not to.
Pick up.

BRICK
Screw retirement.

STEEL ^
(grinning)
Screw retirement, too.

CLOSE ON THE PHONE

> CUT TO:

EXT. ROOFTOP - CONTINUOUS

Wind. A water tower groans.

> THE END <

